{"page": 9, "text": "10 Table of Contents Note 7. Assets Held-for-Sale and Sale of Businesses On September 2, 2025, the Company completed the sale of its aerospace and defense business, which was part of the Industrial segment, for approximately $400 million, subject to customary post-closing adjustments. In connection with the sale, the Company recorded a gain of $115 million and incurred approximately $9 million in transaction related costs, which were recorded in Gain on sale of business and SG&A expenses, respectively, in the Condensed Consolidated Statements of Earnings in the first quarter of fiscal 2026. On January 30, 2026, the Company completed the sale of its product division based in Munich, Germany that makes tools for materials processing, which was part of the Industrial segment. The transaction resulted in a loss of $96 million. The loss was primarily attributable to impairment charges of $105 million recognized within Impairment of assets held-for-sale in the Condensed Consolidated Statements of Earnings (Loss), including $81 million in the fourth quarter of fiscal 2025, $13 million in the first quarter of fiscal 2026 and $11 million in the second quarter of fiscal 2026. These impairment charges were partially offset by a gain of $115 million recorded within Gain on sale of business in the Condensed Consolidated Statements of Earnings (Loss) in the third quarter of fiscal 2026. In fiscal 2026, the Company recorded additional non-cash impairment charges of $64 million related to three entities within the Industrial segment. Two of these entities had already been classified as held-for-sale as of June 30, 2025 and remained classified as held-for-sale during the first and second quarters of fiscal 2026, while the third entity was classified as held-for-sale during the fourth quarter of fiscal 2026 and remains classified as held-for-sale at September 30, 2026. A plan to dispose of this entity was approved by management during the fourth quarter of fiscal 2026 as part of the Company\u2019s strategic realignment and the Company expects to complete the disposal through a sale to a third party within one year of the held-for-sale classification date. Current assets and current liabilities held-for-sale are recorded in Prepaid and other current assets and Other accrued liabilities, respectively, in our Condensed Consolidated Balance Sheets. Noncurrent assets and noncurrent liabilities held-for-sale are recorded in Other assets and Other liabilities, respectively, in our Condensed Consolidated Balance Sheets. Assets and liabilities held-for-sale are in the Industrial segment at both September 30, 2026 and June 30, 2026. Current and noncurrent assets and liabilities classified as held-for-sale as of September 30, 2026 and June 30, 2026 are as follows ($000):\nSeptember 30, 2026 June 30, 2026\nAccounts receivable $ 828 $ 628\nInventories 31,912 31,755\nPrepaid and refundable income taxes 142 119\nPrepaid and other current assets 3,071 3,127\n"}
